 ## Background
-Lipschitz Pruning was introduced in the paper "Lipschitz Pruning: Hierarchical Simplification of Primitive-Based SDFs" [S1]. It addresses the high cost of SDF evaluation in smooth CSG trees by exploiting the 1-Lipschitz property. The method complements far-field culling and is applicable to ray tracing and meshing contexts. Unlike bounding-volume approaches that require boxes extended by the blending radius, Lipschitz Pruning is space-centric and requires no bounding box computation [S1].
